# trafficcams.vancouver.ca — City of Vancouver intersection cameras, second camera source
# alongside DriveBC (drivebc-cameras.http). See docs/add-trafficcams-vancouver.md for the
# full plan; this file exists to record the traps found while measuring the site, before any
# app code exists (Phase 0).

@mapsKey = {{$dotenv AZURE_MAPS_KEY}}

# The undocumented internal endpoint behind the root page's "Find the intersection's pin on
# the map" link. 219 placemarks — coordinates, name, and a link to the intersection's page —
# for 216 pages the root page also lists. This is the *only* practical geolocation source
# (see the geocode traps below); the crawl below is still required because the KML carries no
# image URLs at all, only the site-level pin.
#
# Note the response: `content-disposition: attachment` and `x-aspnet-version: 2.0.50727` — a
# 2005-era ASP.NET app with no documented API. It could disappear; §8.2 of the plan covers the
# fallback.
### KML placemarks
@name kml
GET https://vanmapp1.vancouver.ca/googleKml/traffic_cameras/

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == application/vnd.google-earth.kml+xml; charset=utf-8

# One intersection page. Confirms the shape the crawler depends on: an `<h1 class="display-2">`
# title and `<img src="cameraimages/…">` tags whose `alt` carries the direction (e.g.
# `alt="Boundary Road and E 1st Ave - North"`) — the field to store, not the filename's corner
# letter. See docs/add-trafficcams-vancouver.md §1 for the full parsing rules (whitespace in
# hrefs, case-insensitive paths, the five images with no ` - ` in their alt).
### One intersection page
GET https://trafficcams.vancouver.ca/boundary1.htm

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == text/html

# A live frame. `ETag` + `Last-Modified`, but **no `Cache-Control`** — unlike DriveBC, which
# sets `no-cache` explicitly. Browsers fall back to heuristic freshness here, which is why the
# app's own cache-busting (`?t=` bucketed to the minute) cannot rely on any server-side cache
# header and must be computed independently. The etag is captured for the conditional request
# below rather than hardcoded — each camera refreshes on its own 5-minute offset, so a fixed
# etag value goes stale within minutes of being recorded.
### Live frame
GET https://trafficcams.vancouver.ca/cameraimages/Boundary1stSNorth.jpg

?? status == 200
?? header content-type == image/jpeg

{{
  exports.boundaryEtag = response.headers.etag;
}}

# Conditional GET on the same image, replayed with the `etag` captured above. Confirms the
# server honours `If-None-Match` with a real 304 despite advertising no `Cache-Control` —
# the one caching signal this site does give.
### Live frame, conditional
GET https://trafficcams.vancouver.ca/cameraimages/Boundary1stSNorth.jpg
If-None-Match: {{boundaryEtag}}

?? status == 304

# --- Geocoding traps ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The plan's original query form (`&` substitution + coordinate bias, no city name) was the
# one already used for route waypoints. It fails silently for intersections: it can land in
# the wrong *province* at a confidence level ("Medium") that is indistinguishable from a real
# hit, so the existing `Low`-confidence gate in AzureMapsGeocoder never catches it. The city
# suffix is mandatory; see docs/add-trafficcams-vancouver.md §2 for the full 216-title survey.

# THE TRAP. Unqualified, this resolves to a real Main-St-and-Marine-Dr address — just not
# Vancouver's. `addressLine` echoes back a clean `&` match (the app's only reliable gate) at
# `Medium` confidence, so neither `confidence` nor "does it contain &" catches this alone.
### Unqualified intersection — wrong province, looks like a hit
@name unqualifiedWrongProvince
GET https://atlas.microsoft.com/geocode
  ?api-version=2026-01-01
  &query=Main%20St%20%26%20Marine%20Dr
  &coordinates=-123.1,49.3
  &top=1
  &subscription-key={{mapsKey}}

?? status == 200

# Same query, city-qualified. Lands in Vancouver this time, but at the *wrong* Marine Drive —
# West Vancouver's, near Ambleside, ~13 km from the real Main St & Marine Dr in South
# Vancouver — still at `Medium` confidence. This is the pair the plan's §8.6 refers to: the
# structured and freeform forms disagree with each other here by ~420 m, and neither is
# right. The KML settles it; Azure geocoding is the fallback for sites missing from the KML,
# not the primary source, precisely because of pairs like this one.
### Qualified intersection — right city, still the wrong street
@name qualifiedWrongStreet
GET https://atlas.microsoft.com/geocode
  ?api-version=2026-01-01
  &query=Main%20St%20%26%20Marine%20Dr%2C%20Vancouver%2C%20BC
  &coordinates=-123.1,49.3
  &top=1
  &subscription-key={{mapsKey}}

?? status == 200

# A city-qualified query that *does* land correctly, for contrast — most titles resolve fine
# once qualified (189/216 under this form alone per the plan's survey). The gate is still
# `addressLine` containing `&`; `confidence` (`High` here, `Medium` above) does not reliably
# separate the two.
### Qualified intersection — correct hit
@name qualifiedHit
GET https://atlas.microsoft.com/geocode
  ?api-version=2026-01-01
  &query=Oak%20St%20%26%20W%2010th%20Ave%2C%20Vancouver%2C%20BC
  &coordinates=-123.1,49.3
  &top=1
  &subscription-key={{mapsKey}}

?? status == 200
